# Jena rule: derive :emits from rule predicate text mentioning a diagnostic code.
#
# For every (rule, diagnostic) pair where the rule's free-text predicate
# contains the diagnostic's code as a substring, infer that the rule emits
# the diagnostic.
#
# This is a high-precision pattern: when an author writes "...; otherwise
# the compiler emits M36010" inside a NormativeStatement.predicate, the
# code-mention is intentional. False positives are rare (codes are unique
# strings; a M-code in prose almost always identifies a real link).
#
# Recall is NOT 100% — many rules describe the *condition* a diagnostic
# fires under without naming the code. Those are picked up later by the
# v2.2 LLM-gated emitter rule (inferenceTime: ranks rules by semantic
# similarity to a diagnostic's description).
#
# Backed by the StrContains builtin in kg/java/reasoner/builtins/.

@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix rfc:  <https://aion.savvi.io/ontology/rfc#>.

[emitsFromText:
  (?rule rdf:type rfc:NormativeStatement)
  (?rule rfc:predicate ?text)
  (?diag rdf:type rfc:Diagnostic)
  (?diag rfc:code ?code)
  strContains(?text, ?code)
  ->
  (?rule rfc:emits ?diag)
]
